 {"id": "EFF-1", "title": "P2: autonomy is 1.00 but the agent burned 8 episodes inside Red's House 1F \u2014 measure efficiency, not just escalation", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "The pure-LLM run long_0927_llm posted 594 decisions with 0 escalations and 0 errors, and the honest autonomy ratio reads 1.00 \u2014 while per-episode final maps show ep001-ep008 ALL ended in 'Red's House 1F', the starting house. Eight episodes (about 19 minutes) to walk out of a two-room building, with every decision counted as an unaided success. The autonomy metric is blind to this: a loop that re-decides the same wrong thing scores exactly as well as efficient progress. DIST-1 saw the mirror image (controller reaches Route 1 then wanders back; held only 4/6) and reported direction-locking at 41% of cycles. Done-when: runs report cycle-efficiency (decisions per map transition, and repeated-state/backtrack rate) alongside autonomy, so 'decided unaided' cannot be reported without 'and moved': the S0 baseline's 786.1 escalations-per-transition is the number this must be compared against.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T21:06:10.988705+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-07T07:55:00Z", "commit_hash": "19ef95113750d66ec5dc1699ad6d184372c7384d", "worker_status": "complete", "guard_result": "tier1 PASS 5/5 (worker standalone + foreman re-run: ruff+mypy+104 focused tests)", "ci_result": "pending CI run at tick write", "worker_summary": "Worker gpt-5.6-sol @ openai-codex: _autonomy_counters gains counted decisions_per_map_transition + backtrack_rate (map/tile repeated-state share) with evidence counts; run_autonomy block, summary tail (efficiency: X dec/map-transition, backtrack Y%, n/a forms) and BENCH-1 episode/comparison stamps carry them. RED-first: 7 new tests failed pre-impl. Post: 104 focused passed, ruff clean, mypy clean."